5. Input

Customer Query: {customer_query}

6. Allowed Outputs

Return exactly ONE of the following nine categories:

Delivery Shipping Refund Payment Cancellation Defect Return Account Unknown

7. Strict Output Constraints
Return exactly one category word.
Preserve the exact spelling and capitalization.
Do not provide explanations or reasoning.
Do not include punctuation or quotation marks.
Never return multiple categories.
Never create additional categories.
Do not classify based only on keywords.
Do not assume missing information.
Never classify a meaningful query as Unknown merely because of spelling or grammar mistakes.
Always understand the customer's complete intention and context.
Final Instruction

Think through the complete customer query internally. Identify the actual problem, check the context, understand the requested solution, and apply the classification rules.

Return ONLY the most appropriate category name from the nine allowed outputs.
